{
  "id": "v2-r01-t05",
  "repoId": "owned-v2-r01",
  "split": "development",
  "title": "Count adjacent list runs independently",
  "description": "This ListWeave snapshot contains runs(values), a compact representation of consecutive repeated list items for in-memory display summaries. A counting refactor merged separate runs of the same value. Restore the adjacent-run contract for JSON data, with finite numbers and JavaScript-safe integers.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R01",
      "text": "For list values, runs returns one {\"value\": first_item, \"count\": positive_integer} object for each maximal contiguous Python == run, in order. Nonadjacent equal values stay separate. Equality is recursive for lists and dictionaries, exact for strings without Unicode normalization, and includes Python numeric equality True == 1 and False == 0. Each run retains its first item as value; None and empty nested containers are supported. Empty input returns []."
    },
    {
      "id": "R02",
      "text": "For list input, runs leaves the caller list and all nested lists and dictionaries unchanged, including repeated values in separate runs."
    },
    {
      "id": "R03",
      "text": "A non-list values of any JSON type, including None, raises TypeError."
    }
  ],
  "files": {
    "runs.py": "# ListWeave: original synthetic list-maintenance module. CC0-1.0.\ndef runs(values):\n    if not isinstance(values, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"expected a list\")\n    groups = []\n    for value in values:\n        if not any(value == group[\"value\"] for group in groups):\n            groups.append({\"value\": value, \"count\": values.count(value)})\n    return groups\n"
  },
  "editAllowlist": [
    "runs.py"
  ],
